Simplified the package by removing the last nonessential helper classes and keeping the API centered on `KMPSearch`.

What changed:
- Moved the sample constants into [KMPSearch.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/021_kmp_pattern_searching/kmp/KMPSearch.java).
- Removed [KmpExamples.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/021_kmp_pattern_searching/kmp/KmpExamples.java).
- Removed [KmpFormatter.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/021_kmp_pattern_searching/kmp/KmpFormatter.java).
- Kept [KmpMatcher.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/021_kmp_pattern_searching/kmp/KmpMatcher.java) as the internal engine and simplified its return path.
- Updated [KmpMatcherTest.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/021_kmp_pattern_searching/kmp/KmpMatcherTest.java) to use local test fixtures and assert the returned list is immutable.

Why this is better:
- Fewer files and fewer helper abstractions.
- The package now has a tighter shape: one public facade, one internal matcher, one test.
- The sample CLI logic no longer depends on separate formatting/example classes.

Verification:
- `javac kmp/*.java` succeeded.
- `java -cp . kmp.KMPSearch` printed `0 9 12`.
- `java -cp . kmp.KmpMatcherTest` printed `All KMP matcher tests passed.`

If you want, I can keep going with one of these:
1. Add a small README with usage and algorithm notes.
2. Make the CLI accept input from stdin when no arguments are provided.
3. Add a few more edge-case tests for repeated-prefix patterns.

