Refactored the KMP implementation into a cleaner, standard Java entry point in [KMPSearch.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/021_kmp_pattern_searching/KMPSearch.java).

What changed:
- Aligned the public class name with the filename so `java KMPSearch` works normally.
- Extracted LPS construction into a dedicated `buildLps` helper.
- Added null and empty-input guards to avoid runtime exceptions on edge cases.
- Kept the existing `search(String pat, String txt)` API returning `ArrayList<Integer>` to preserve compatibility.
- Simplified the sample output formatting.

Verification:
- `javac KMPSearch.java` succeeded.
- `java KMPSearch` now prints `0 9 12`.

I removed the old mismatched source file [kmp_pattern_searching.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/021_kmp_pattern_searching/kmp_pattern_searching.java) as part of the cleanup.

